  "id": "npc_schedule.mira_sen",
  "note": "Mira studies at home each school morning (07:00-09:30), walks 20 minutes to school (arrives 09:50 for the 10:00 assembly), is in Class XI Commerce until the 15:50 last bell, then on Tuesday and Thursday walks 40 minutes to the stationery shop and helps her mother at the packing desk from 16:30 to 18:00 (the customer counter is Anindita's anchor; the packing desk is Mira's, so they never share an anchor), and walks home (28 minutes). On Monday, Wednesday and Friday her afternoon is her own: she goes to location.nabapara.mira_out (an authored off-lane leg, 18 minutes from school) until 18:00 and walks home (11 minutes). Saturday is lighter study and her own plans out of the house from 11:00 to 16:00; Sunday stays at home. Evening study 20:00-21:30, home from 21:30, asleep from 22:30 on every day. location.nabapara.school is the lane-schedule zone for Nabapara Vidyalaya; the attendance system keeps its own rooms (nhss.room_xi_commerce) and the integrator maps one to the other. The desk, counter and door routes are the same built polylines as Anindita's file (727, 1100 and 2000 cm). The school, mira_out and school-to-door legs are authored off-lane lengths. Every travel duration is ceil(sum(lengthCm)/140).",
